and after what Chuck Todd did

00:30:39.180 --> 00:30:41.410
in the last couple weeks with Bob Barr,

00:30:41.410 --> 00:30:43.030
and just like watching the rest of it,

00:30:43.030 --> 00:30:44.630
it's like, you know what,

00:30:44.630 --> 00:30:46.410
maybe just let it crumble.

00:30:46.410 --> 00:30:48.920
And while I think there's
major risks on the other side,

00:30:48.920 --> 00:30:50.760
if we have nothing that's mainstream,

00:30:50.760 --> 00:30:53.330
it's like what gives us national cohesion?

00:30:53.330 --> 00:30:55.050
It's like why are we saving this thing?

00:30:55.050 --> 00:30:56.410
Are you in that space?

00:30:56.410 --> 00:30:58.170
Or do you think there's
something worth saving

00:30:58.170 --> 00:31:00.300
or some mix, maybe?

00:31:00.300 --> 00:31:01.920
- Yeah, I think it's kind of a mix.

00:31:01.920 --> 00:31:05.250
I don't ever think that the
press has been unbiased ever

00:31:05.250 --> 00:31:06.960
even since its inception.

00:31:06.960 --> 00:31:09.770
I mean, I think of the funny little ways

00:31:09.770 --> 00:31:10.850
that they used to,

00:31:10.850 --> 00:31:13.017
like during the days of our founding

00:31:13.017 --> 00:31:15.930
that folks would go after each other,

00:31:15.930 --> 00:31:18.270
politicians would write nasty editorials,

00:31:18.270 --> 00:31:20.250
which were so much more
scandalous than some

00:31:20.250 --> 00:31:22.811
of the stuff that we're seeing now.

00:31:22.811 --> 00:31:23.644
- He's got syphilis.

00:31:23.644 --> 00:31:25.910
It's like a whole bunch of crazy stuff.

00:31:25.910 --> 00:31:28.280
- Like real colonial
housewives come to life.

00:31:28.280 --> 00:31:30.210
That's what it seemed like,

00:31:30.210 --> 00:31:32.480
it was so crazy.

00:31:32.480 --> 00:31:34.750
I don't think that they've
ever been unbiased.

00:31:34.750 --> 00:31:37.790
I do think that they maybe
perhaps have been a little bit

00:31:37.790 --> 00:31:39.560
more attentive to the needs of the people

00:31:39.560 --> 00:31:40.550
because at one point,

00:31:40.550 --> 00:31:41.640
the press was the people,

00:31:41.640 --> 00:31:44.410
the press and the people
kind of were hand in hand,

00:31:44.410 --> 00:31:46.430
and the press was the people's way

00:31:46.430 --> 00:31:48.130
to keep check on their government.

00:31:48.130 --> 00:31:52.070
And now, it's dissolved
into party allegiances.

00:31:52.070 --> 00:31:53.470
And a lot of the press,

00:31:53.470 --> 00:31:54.640
and there have been surveys,

00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:57.260
the majority of them identify politically

00:31:57.260 --> 00:31:58.810
one way as opposed to the other.

00:31:58.810 --> 00:32:00.890
And I don't even have a problem with that.

00:32:00.890 --> 00:32:03.150
The problem that I have is the egos

00:32:03.150 --> 00:32:05.770
of so many of these
individuals who seem to think

00:32:05.770 --> 00:32:08.950
that the byline isn't
the most important thing

00:32:08.950 --> 00:32:09.860
on a piece,

00:32:09.860 --> 00:32:12.690
as opposed to the information
that the piece is sharing

00:32:12.690 --> 00:32:14.210
and or supposed to share.

00:32:14.210 --> 00:32:18.360
And so many of these Q&amp;As
with the president turn into

00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:19.410
some kind of footage

00:32:19.410 --> 00:32:23.170
for a reporter to aggrandize themselves

00:32:23.170 --> 00:32:25.380
and make a story out of themselves

00:32:25.380 --> 00:32:28.650
or it's all prop, it's
political propaganda.

00:32:28.650 --> 00:32:31.980
And it's frustrating
because I always feel,

00:32:31.980 --> 00:32:34.550
a free press is a sacred thing.

00:32:34.550 --> 00:32:37.900
And I will defend that to the end.

00:32:37.900 --> 00:32:39.300
But are they free, though,

00:32:39.300 --> 00:32:42.770
when they cannot report on things outside

00:32:42.770 --> 00:32:44.480
of that political filter,

00:32:44.480 --> 00:32:47.530
when everything has to run
through that party affiliation?

00:32:47.530 --> 00:32:49.590
Is that really free reporting?

00:32:49.590 --> 00:32:53.090
And I also think that
criticism of the press seems

00:32:53.090 --> 00:32:54.520
to be taboo now.

00:32:54.520 --> 00:32:57.610
But a lot of people in the
press don't seem to understand

00:32:57.610 --> 00:33:00.380
that a free press and
a free people's right

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:01.720
to criticize their free press,

00:33:01.720 --> 00:33:03.090
these are things that go hand in hand,

00:33:03.090 --> 00:33:04.830
you can't have one without the other.

00:33:04.830 --> 00:33:07.620
And you can't criticize
our criticism of you

00:33:07.620 --> 00:33:10.403
without kind of ultimately
betraying your principles.

00:33:12.470 --> 00:33:16.870
Like I said, I don't mind
bias when it's honest.

00:33:16.870 --> 00:33:20.220
But I don't want people
to report something

00:33:20.220 --> 00:33:22.730
and have it be politically one sided

00:33:22.730 --> 00:33:25.890
and then try to rely on the credit earned

00:33:25.890 --> 00:33:28.140
by a previous media generation back

00:33:28.140 --> 00:33:30.170
when they at least attempted to not place

00:33:30.170 --> 00:33:32.030
so much emphasis on the byline,

00:33:32.030 --> 00:33:34.883
or who was anchoring the news
at that particular point.

00:33:36.260 --> 00:33:39.010
I wish that they would just
focus on the information.

00:33:39.010 --> 00:33:41.160
And if they want to do
editorial, do editorial.

00:33:41.160 --> 00:33:42.550
Like I'm not a journalist,

00:33:42.550 --> 00:33:44.852
I'm not a hard reporter.

00:33:44.852 --> 00:33:48.270
I am an editorialist,
commentator, an analyst.

00:33:48.270 --> 00:33:50.660
I am so biased, it's crazy,

00:33:50.660 --> 00:33:51.690
but I admit it,

00:33:51.690 --> 00:33:53.730
and I'll be honest with people about it,

00:33:53.730 --> 00:33:57.054
but I want them to do the same as well.

00:33:57.054 --> 00:33:59.460
Just be honest about it.

00:33:59.460 --> 00:34:01.550
- Do you think people get confused

00:34:01.550 --> 00:34:03.430
when people attack the media?

00:34:03.430 --> 00:34:05.340
There seems to be this idea
that if people like you

00:34:05.340 --> 00:34:07.040
and I attack the media,

00:34:07.040 --> 00:34:09.930
that somehow we're part of the problem.

00:34:09.930 --> 00:34:11.650
Or the other version of this is like

00:34:11.650 --> 00:34:13.640
when Trump fights with everyone at CNN,

00:34:13.640 --> 00:34:15.250
he's fighting with Jim Acosta.

00:34:15.250 --> 00:34:17.720
And people are like,
he's attacking the press.

00:34:17.720 --> 00:34:18.553
And it's like, well,

00:34:18.553 --> 00:34:19.780
I actually have no problem with that,

00:34:19.780 --> 00:34:21.480
he has first amendment rights, too.

00:34:21.480 --> 00:34:24.560
Now if he was using the power
of the government, obviously,

00:34:24.560 --> 00:34:25.393
to silence them,

00:34:25.393 --> 00:34:27.360
well, now we got a problem.

00:34:27.360 --> 00:34:28.710
But he, as far as I know,

00:34:28.710 --> 00:34:29.880
he's not doing that.

00:34:29.880 --> 00:34:32.000
Yet they love to play the victim too.

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:34.830
And it's like, what happens
in America constantly,

00:34:34.830 --> 00:34:36.430
is that everyone is exercising

00:34:36.430 --> 00:34:38.030
their free speech all the time.

00:34:38.030 --> 00:34:40.830
I mean, we could get to
the big tech problem,

00:34:40.830 --> 00:34:41.663
maybe in a moment,

00:34:41.663 --> 00:34:44.670
but like that the way
it actually is working,

00:34:44.670 --> 00:34:45.770
Trump fighting with them,

00:34:45.770 --> 00:34:47.020
them attacking Trump,

00:34:47.020 --> 00:34:48.490
us attacking them,

00:34:48.490 --> 00:34:50.060
you may not love the whole game,

00:34:50.060 --> 00:34:53.330
and it may be something
that burns too hot,

00:34:53.330 --> 00:34:55.630
so it's eventually gonna
explode or something.

00:34:55.630 --> 00:34:57.180
But like everyone's free speech

00:34:57.180 --> 00:35:01.160
is being protected basically.

00:35:01.160 --> 00:35:02.480
- No, I think that's a good point.

00:35:02.480 --> 00:35:04.600
I mean, isn't that what it's all about?

00:35:04.600 --> 00:35:06.620
I mean, America has always been kind of

00:35:06.620 --> 00:35:09.420
like a big giant family
arguing at the dinner table.

00:35:09.420 --> 00:35:11.310
And it makes it infuriating,

00:35:11.310 --> 00:35:12.520
but also amazing.

00:35:12.520 --> 00:35:14.150
I mean, I wouldn't
change it for the world.

00:35:14.150 --> 00:35:16.010
And that's what it's supposed to be like,

00:35:16.010 --> 00:35:19.230
but this idea that if you criticize

00:35:20.190 --> 00:35:22.080
the press for bad reporting,

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:24.470
and there are numerous
examples of bad reporting.

00:35:24.470 --> 00:35:27.560
There are entire media
entities on the right

00:35:27.560 --> 00:35:32.060
that exist to document legitimate
cases of bias reporting.

00:35:32.060 --> 00:35:34.870
And that's not attacking anyone,

00:35:34.870 --> 00:35:36.500
they act like they're on a battlefield

00:35:36.500 --> 00:35:38.810
and as they're trying to eat their MRE,

00:35:38.810 --> 00:35:41.620
they're being hit with
missiles from the President

00:35:41.620 --> 00:35:43.610
or from a Republican or whatever,

00:35:43.610 --> 00:35:46.480
because they dared to write a bad story.

00:35:46.480 --> 00:35:48.240
And that's the point of it.

00:35:48.240 --> 00:35:49.760
It's like we also in addition

00:35:49.760 --> 00:35:50.990
to keeping our politicians honest,

00:35:50.990 --> 00:35:52.430
we have to keep our press honest.

00:35:52.430 --> 00:35:54.190
And I feel like we were sold a bad,

00:35:54.190 --> 00:35:55.490
that was a bad sale.

00:35:55.490 --> 00:35:57.860
Like we were supposed
to have them as an ally

00:35:57.860 --> 00:36:00.700
instead of now because
really there are a lot

00:36:00.700 --> 00:36:01.533
of people in the press,

00:36:01.533 --> 00:36:02.800
and I know you would agree with this,

00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:05.510
that have really abused
their position of power.

00:36:05.510 --> 00:36:07.870
And it is a position of power.

00:36:07.870 --> 00:36:10.710
I will never forget the
story of this elderly lady,

00:36:10.710 --> 00:36:12.550
and I wrote about it in my book,

00:36:12.550 --> 00:36:15.090
this elderly woman who
had a Facebook group

00:36:15.090 --> 00:36:16.810
that was a pro Trump Facebook group.

00:36:16.810 --> 00:36:18.160
I mean, she can do whatever she wants,

00:36:18.160 --> 00:36:19.000
she can play FarmVille,

00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:21.190
she can do a pro Trump Facebook group.

00:36:21.190 --> 00:36:24.520
And CNN showed up at her house

00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:26.790
and they did a story on her.

00:36:26.790 --> 00:36:29.450
Her address was displayed on camera

00:36:29.450 --> 00:36:31.580
and she ended up getting threats.

00:36:31.580 --> 00:36:33.320
And I'm thinking

00:36:33.320 --> 00:36:35.520
because you don't like
a political affiliation,

00:36:35.520 --> 00:36:37.420
you decide to abuse
your authority as a way

00:36:37.420 --> 00:36:41.890
to really intimidate
people into not engaging

00:36:41.890 --> 00:36:43.743
in a right that they have.

00:36:44.670 --> 00:36:45.770
That's bothersome.

00:36:45.770 --> 00:36:47.880
I've been the victim of press bias.

00:36:47.880 --> 00:36:49.850
You've been the victim of press bias.

00:36:49.850 --> 00:36:51.240
I don't think there's anyone that is

00:36:51.240 --> 00:36:53.870
in this industry that
hasn't been affected.

00:36:53.870 --> 00:36:56.440
But the idea that any kind of criticism

00:36:56.440 --> 00:36:59.000
of them means that they
are being persecuted,

00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:00.650
I would have to say, well,

00:37:00.650 --> 00:37:03.010
there is a definitive history as to

00:37:03.010 --> 00:37:05.200
who started what.

00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:06.540
And it wasn't the people

00:37:06.540 --> 00:37:08.860
who attacked an unbiased press.

00:37:08.860 --> 00:37:10.650
It was the people who started pointing out

00:37:10.650 --> 00:37:12.630
some really unfair and nasty articles

00:37:12.630 --> 00:37:13.463
that had been written.

00:37:13.463 --> 00:37:16.370
So I don't give a lot of credence.

00:37:16.370 --> 00:37:18.240
And when they're unfairly attacked,

00:37:18.240 --> 00:37:19.810
I'll definitely speak up.

00:37:19.810 --> 00:37:22.750
But not every one of
those attacks are unfair,

00:37:22.750 --> 00:37:25.170
or criticisms are unfair.

00:37:25.170 --> 00:37:26.690
- So that's actually a perfect segue

00:37:26.690 --> 00:37:28.000
to the outrage part of this.

00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:30.610
So as I'm doing all my press for my book,

00:37:30.610 --> 00:37:33.770
one of the things that people
are asking me constantly

00:37:33.770 --> 00:37:36.620
is when did the outrage thing start?

00:37:36.620 --> 00:37:38.670
Is there a moment that you can point to

00:37:38.670 --> 00:37:40.000
that it started.

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:42.070
I have a couple different answers for it,

00:37:42.070 --> 00:37:45.000
'cause I think there's a few
things that led up to it.

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:46.990
But do you see like a moment

00:37:46.990 --> 00:37:49.247
or a political movement or a person

00:37:49.247 --> 00:37:53.343
that sort of got us into this
mess that now we all see?

00:37:54.610 --> 00:37:56.250
- Oh, that's a good question,

00:37:56.250 --> 00:37:59.380
because it feels like people
have been outraged for so long.

00:37:59.380 --> 00:38:01.890
Even since the George W. Bush years,

00:38:01.890 --> 00:38:03.500
even maybe even going back to Reagan,

00:38:03.500 --> 00:38:06.750
people have been outraged for a long time.

00:38:06.750 --> 00:38:07.810
I remember going,

00:38:07.810 --> 00:38:10.400
the first time I was ever
at the Reagan Library,

00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:13.120
and I was looking at one of the exhibits

00:38:13.120 --> 00:38:14.930
and it was about some of the media bias

00:38:14.930 --> 00:38:17.550
towards Reagan and those
headlines were nasty.

00:38:17.550 --> 00:38:19.220
And he would say one thing

00:38:19.220 --> 00:38:21.030
or look one particular way

00:38:21.030 --> 00:38:22.800
and there were headlines about it.

00:38:22.800 --> 00:38:24.600
I do think that it's grown

00:38:24.600 --> 00:38:27.490
to include almost every aspect of life.

00:38:27.490 --> 00:38:31.563
So instead of it just being a
reaction, it's now a culture.

00:38:32.420 --> 00:38:33.933
And when that occurred,

00:38:35.950 --> 00:38:38.290
I don't know, maybe sometime
after George W. Bush,

00:38:38.290 --> 00:38:40.390
it's one of those things where
it's been around for so long,

00:38:40.390 --> 00:38:42.330
we don't realize that we are in it,

00:38:42.330 --> 00:38:45.070
we don't realize how
long we've been in it.

00:38:45.070 --> 00:38:47.410
When do you think it started?

00:38:47.410 --> 00:38:49.500
- So I have a couple of
different answers on this

00:38:49.500 --> 00:38:51.313
but i think,

00:38:51.313 --> 00:38:52.610
you know my story, so as a lefty,

00:38:52.610 --> 00:38:54.890
I was very much in like
the progressive thing

00:38:54.890 --> 00:38:57.250
and I think it was sort of

00:38:57.250 --> 00:38:59.420
the first time Bernie came around.

00:38:59.420 --> 00:39:00.700
He ignited,

00:39:00.700 --> 00:39:03.550
although I don't think
he himself was realizing

00:39:03.550 --> 00:39:05.360
what he was doing exactly.

00:39:05.360 --> 00:39:07.170
He ignited this like thing

00:39:07.170 --> 00:39:08.700
that was laying underneath this,

00:39:08.700 --> 00:39:11.370
like there was tinder
basically underneath,

00:39:11.370 --> 00:39:15.360
that he ignited that sort of
everything in America was bad.

00:39:15.360 --> 00:39:17.090
And that once you do that,

00:39:17.090 --> 00:39:20.550
you couple that with identity politics,

00:39:20.550 --> 00:39:25.260
you couple that with 20
years or almost three decades

00:39:25.260 --> 00:39:27.700
maybe of kids being told
that they can never lose

00:39:27.700 --> 00:39:30.450
and their feelings matter
and participation, trophies,

00:39:30.450 --> 00:39:33.000
and basically all of these things,

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:35.870
that then as we became
more hyper partisan,

00:39:35.870 --> 00:39:36.703
and then you finally,

00:39:36.703 --> 00:39:38.280
you throw Trump onto it,

00:39:38.280 --> 00:39:40.250
which I think he was
just the symptom of it,

00:39:40.250 --> 00:39:41.550
not the cause of it.

00:39:41.550 --> 00:39:43.770
But that I think is why
the last five years,

00:39:43.770 --> 00:39:46.000
oh, and then of course, you
throw social media into it.

00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:48.120
So I don't know that
there's an exact moment,

00:39:48.120 --> 00:39:52.130
but it was like hyper
partisan leftyness coupled

00:39:52.130 --> 00:39:54.960
with sort of the collapse
of the decent liberal,

00:39:54.960 --> 00:39:57.180
you throw in social media,
you throw in trolls,

00:39:57.180 --> 00:39:58.060
you throw in bots,

00:39:58.060 --> 00:40:00.550
you throw in Trump who
wants to play that game.

00:40:00.550 --> 00:40:02.230
You throw in the dishonest media

00:40:02.230 --> 00:40:06.050
and it was almost like
we summoned this thing.

00:40:06.050 --> 00:40:07.370
We all sort of did it together.

00:40:07.370 --> 00:40:08.460
I don't point to like, oh,

00:40:08.460 --> 00:40:11.520
it was April 25th, 2007.

00:40:11.520 --> 00:40:12.800
- We summoned a monster.

00:40:12.800 --> 00:40:15.440
It is very much a Frankenstein's
monster kind of story.

00:40:15.440 --> 00:40:17.490
And you're right, social
media intensifies it,

00:40:17.490 --> 00:40:19.130
it's the magnifying glass

00:40:19.130 --> 00:40:21.440
through which the sun's rays are leveled

00:40:21.440 --> 00:40:22.950
at some of our fellow ants.

00:40:22.950 --> 00:40:25.350
I mean, that's really
ultimately what it's like.

00:40:26.763 --> 00:40:29.440
I definitely think that
the Bernie thing ushered in

00:40:29.440 --> 00:40:31.350
the whole outrages of culture

00:40:31.350 --> 00:40:33.930
because it existed as a tactic,

00:40:33.930 --> 00:40:35.250
and I remember even seeing it during

00:40:35.250 --> 00:40:37.340
the Occupy Wall Street days.

00:40:37.340 --> 00:40:40.940
But definitely with the introduction

00:40:40.940 --> 00:40:44.490
as not just a Bernie
Sanders but of socialism

00:40:44.490 --> 00:40:47.420
as now kind of like a
legitimate spring off

00:40:47.420 --> 00:40:48.930
of the Democrat Party,

00:40:48.930 --> 00:40:50.670
or really ultimately
what the Democrat Party

00:40:50.670 --> 00:40:54.060
is now, it really hasn't taken over.

00:40:54.060 --> 00:40:55.950
And there isn't a good,

00:40:55.950 --> 00:40:57.390
what happened to the liberals?

00:40:57.390 --> 00:40:58.600
Where did the liberals go?

00:40:58.600 --> 00:41:01.650
Where did those liberal
that were Democrats,

00:41:01.650 --> 00:41:03.750
like even the Joe Manchin's kind,

00:41:03.750 --> 00:41:05.450
I mean he seems like a decent guy.

00:41:05.450 --> 00:41:07.840
I disagree with him on a
number of policy issues.

00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:09.510
But he seems like a decent guy, right?

00:41:09.510 --> 00:41:11.460
He's not a nasty person.

00:41:11.460 --> 00:41:13.560
He really focuses on policy,

00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:16.530
but he's like a dinosaur
in the Democrat Party.

00:41:16.530 --> 00:41:19.460
It's not cool to be kind.

00:41:19.460 --> 00:41:21.907
I mean, it really isn't, it's not.

00:41:21.907 --> 00:41:22.993
I mean that's true.

00:41:24.441 --> 00:41:26.810
- As I said to you on
your show the other day,

00:41:26.810 --> 00:41:30.053
they basically executed
Order 66 on the liberals.

