00:52:28.260 --> 00:52:29.093
in our world.

00:52:29.093 --> 00:52:30.710
Or maybe it does and
we just don't know it.

00:52:30.710 --> 00:52:32.960
Maybe that's what those
UFO videos are about.

00:52:35.060 --> 00:52:38.750
It doesn't prevent bad guys
from coming into the area.

00:52:38.750 --> 00:52:40.660
They're not gonna show up illegally

00:52:40.660 --> 00:52:42.350
in possession of a firearm.

00:52:42.350 --> 00:52:43.930
And I hate the phrase illegal guns.

00:52:43.930 --> 00:52:45.520
It's always illegal possession.

00:52:45.520 --> 00:52:46.400
They're not gonna show up

00:52:46.400 --> 00:52:47.457
with an illegally possessed gun and go,

00:52:47.457 --> 00:52:48.867
"You know what, I was gonna go in here

00:52:48.867 --> 00:52:50.710
"and do some really shady stuff."

00:52:50.710 --> 00:52:55.083
But this sticker, no, I'm
not totally on the sticker.

00:52:56.400 --> 00:52:57.270
That's never happened.

00:52:57.270 --> 00:53:00.270
And John Lott who is a
walking encyclopedia,

00:53:00.270 --> 00:53:02.850
he's done a lot of research on
this. And I think what is it,

00:53:02.850 --> 00:53:05.960
like the vast majority of
mass casualty incidents,

00:53:05.960 --> 00:53:08.270
these mass shootings that have taken place

00:53:08.270 --> 00:53:11.740
from the period of 1953
till current time have been

00:53:11.740 --> 00:53:13.770
in gun free zones.

00:53:13.770 --> 00:53:15.270
And a lot of these gun free zones,

00:53:15.270 --> 00:53:19.930
they don't even have
armed security to protect

00:53:19.930 --> 00:53:21.690
or at least try to protect the people

00:53:21.690 --> 00:53:22.920
that they allow to come in.

00:53:22.920 --> 00:53:27.160
So that is like Linus' blanket.

00:53:27.160 --> 00:53:28.580
It's a safety blanket.

00:53:28.580 --> 00:53:30.710
This idea of a gun-free anything,

00:53:30.710 --> 00:53:32.020
why don't you just put a sign up

00:53:32.020 --> 00:53:33.080
that says crime free.

00:53:33.080 --> 00:53:34.650
Is some crime acceptable to you?

00:53:34.650 --> 00:53:38.030
Just put a crime free zone sticker,

00:53:38.030 --> 00:53:39.020
it's never worked.

00:53:39.020 --> 00:53:41.260
We live in a reality where,

00:53:41.260 --> 00:53:43.870
and this is why I think
some freedom scares people.

00:53:43.870 --> 00:53:48.010
Some people cannot handle freedom

00:53:48.010 --> 00:53:50.820
because they don't, I
think, trust themselves

00:53:50.820 --> 00:53:52.730
and they don't trust other people.

00:53:52.730 --> 00:53:54.830
And there are going to be people

00:53:54.830 --> 00:53:57.000
that are going to abuse their freedom.

00:53:57.000 --> 00:54:00.100
And even after they have been caught

00:54:00.100 --> 00:54:01.610
and they have faced justice

00:54:01.610 --> 00:54:03.060
and they have been punished,

00:54:03.060 --> 00:54:05.210
they're still going to reoffend

00:54:05.210 --> 00:54:07.740
and they're still going
to choose to do bad things

00:54:07.740 --> 00:54:08.973
with their freewill.

00:54:10.160 --> 00:54:12.870
You're never gonna be able
to legislate evil away,

00:54:12.870 --> 00:54:17.870
because you cannot legislate
that away in each individual.

00:54:18.060 --> 00:54:23.060
And the solution isn't to
remove people's ability

00:54:24.640 --> 00:54:26.010
to defend themselves.

00:54:26.010 --> 00:54:28.570
The solution is to make criminals afraid,

00:54:28.570 --> 00:54:31.300
with more severe penalties instead of,

00:54:31.300 --> 00:54:32.340
I mean, I could sit here and talk to you

00:54:32.340 --> 00:54:34.010
about our justice system on and on and on,

00:54:34.010 --> 00:54:35.590
because I think we have a massive problem

00:54:35.590 --> 00:54:37.110
and we have too many felonies

00:54:37.110 --> 00:54:40.550
and some of the non violent,
it just goes on and on.

00:54:40.550 --> 00:54:42.460
But for the serious offenders,

00:54:42.460 --> 00:54:43.670
there needs to be penalties

00:54:43.670 --> 00:54:46.300
that really are adequate deterrence,

00:54:46.300 --> 00:54:48.880
and quit punishing the law abiding

00:54:48.880 --> 00:54:51.620
for what these people choose to freely do.

00:54:51.620 --> 00:54:52.860
And I always tell people,

00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:54.910
there are no such thing as loopholes.

00:54:54.910 --> 00:54:58.010
It's like if someone is caught
driving under the influence,

00:54:58.010 --> 00:54:59.380
they have their license suspended

00:54:59.380 --> 00:55:04.380
and they continue going
and driving a vehicle,

00:55:04.420 --> 00:55:05.290
they get caught.

00:55:05.290 --> 00:55:06.450
That's not a loophole.

00:55:06.450 --> 00:55:07.283
They're breaking the law.

00:55:07.283 --> 00:55:08.440
That's a criminal act.

00:55:08.440 --> 00:55:10.520
So these loopholes that
people keep talking about,

00:55:10.520 --> 00:55:12.920
there's criminal acts
and non-criminal acts.

00:55:12.920 --> 00:55:14.120
There's no nuance there.

00:55:14.120 --> 00:55:16.420
The ATF has things covered to the point

00:55:16.420 --> 00:55:18.448
of being over covered.

00:55:18.448 --> 00:55:20.300
So there's a criminal act,

00:55:20.300 --> 00:55:21.870
and then there's a non-criminal act,

00:55:21.870 --> 00:55:23.690
there's no loophole.

00:55:23.690 --> 00:55:26.420
- We always hear about
the gun show loophole.

00:55:26.420 --> 00:55:28.050
- I know the gun show loophole,

00:55:28.050 --> 00:55:30.070
because you always have gang members

00:55:30.070 --> 00:55:31.180
they have going out there

00:55:31.180 --> 00:55:35.100
and buying super expensive
collector's guns,

00:55:35.100 --> 00:55:37.240
and then going out and
committing all of these crimes

00:55:37.240 --> 00:55:38.520
with collector's items.

00:55:38.520 --> 00:55:39.560
And even that is even,

00:55:39.560 --> 00:55:41.100
even private sales are regulated

00:55:41.100 --> 00:55:45.440
to a point and the penalty
on that is incredibly high.

00:55:45.440 --> 00:55:46.660
But that's not how,

00:55:46.660 --> 00:55:48.840
I mean, gangbangers, they've
done surveys on this,

00:55:48.840 --> 00:55:50.290
people who are committing
crimes are getting this

00:55:50.290 --> 00:55:51.370
off the black market.

00:55:51.370 --> 00:55:53.820
And if you think you're gonna
eradicate the black market,

00:55:53.820 --> 00:55:55.470
I mean, look how well the
war on drugs has gone.

00:55:55.470 --> 00:55:57.050
You think that this is
gonna be any different.

00:55:57.050 --> 00:55:59.450
I mean, it's the same
thing, different variable.

00:56:00.490 --> 00:56:04.300
- Are you hopeful for
America at this point,

00:56:04.300 --> 00:56:06.720
like we can talk about all the scary stuff

00:56:06.720 --> 00:56:09.300
and the frustrations and
young people have problems,

00:56:09.300 --> 00:56:10.360
and the media is collapsing,

00:56:10.360 --> 00:56:13.760
and it feels like our institutions
are crumbling and COVID.

00:56:13.760 --> 00:56:16.913
And we don't have trusted
sources, like all of this stuff.

00:56:18.220 --> 00:56:22.250
But I sense that underneath
that is some hope

00:56:22.250 --> 00:56:23.880
or some grace.

00:56:23.880 --> 00:56:28.660
- I like to market myself
as a perpetual cynic.

00:56:28.660 --> 00:56:30.850
And I think it just comes
by way of being like,

00:56:30.850 --> 00:56:32.020
young Gen X.

00:56:32.020 --> 00:56:33.030
I just am a cynic.

00:56:33.030 --> 00:56:35.690
And that's like the Gen X
thing, is to be cynical.

00:56:35.690 --> 00:56:40.690
But I have a supreme
appreciation and fondness

00:56:41.350 --> 00:56:44.550
for that crazy American spirit,

00:56:44.550 --> 00:56:46.817
the spirit that drove people to go,

00:56:46.817 --> 00:56:48.807
"Hey, let's just take a wagon and go out

00:56:48.807 --> 00:56:49.640
"in the wilderness."

00:56:49.640 --> 00:56:51.020
We have no idea what's gonna happen,

00:56:51.020 --> 00:56:54.680
but we're just gonna just
create something out there.

00:56:54.680 --> 00:56:58.830
It is an animating spirit of liberty

00:56:58.830 --> 00:57:01.010
and it makes people courageous

00:57:01.010 --> 00:57:04.270
and it has made this country
in such a short period of time,

00:57:04.270 --> 00:57:05.600
this beacon on the hill,

00:57:05.600 --> 00:57:07.960
this amazing thing.

00:57:07.960 --> 00:57:11.230
And I'm hopeful because of that.

00:57:11.230 --> 00:57:13.490
And I even think,

00:57:13.490 --> 00:57:17.081
even with some of the progressives
out there, you'll notice,

00:57:17.081 --> 00:57:18.400
they're critical of,

00:57:18.400 --> 00:57:19.640
even though they're leftist,

00:57:19.640 --> 00:57:20.590
and some of them are socialist,

00:57:20.590 --> 00:57:22.840
and some of say that they're communists,

00:57:22.840 --> 00:57:23.810
they're all pretty critical

00:57:23.810 --> 00:57:24.850
of Communist China.

00:57:24.850 --> 00:57:26.420
They're pretty critical of Xi Jinping.

00:57:26.420 --> 00:57:29.400
So there is still something
in that American DNA

00:57:29.400 --> 00:57:33.630
that is making them rebel against at least

00:57:33.630 --> 00:57:35.713
somewhat against authoritarianism.

00:57:36.891 --> 00:57:38.910
The news looks bad.

00:57:38.910 --> 00:57:42.500
I just know that media
likes selling you bad news.

00:57:42.500 --> 00:57:44.290
So I don't really pay
any attention to that.

00:57:44.290 --> 00:57:47.110
But I'm hopeful because of the stuff

00:57:47.110 --> 00:57:48.900
that I see in little bits

00:57:48.900 --> 00:57:50.710
that doesn't get reported.

00:57:50.710 --> 00:57:52.520
The story of the guy who goes around

00:57:52.520 --> 00:57:54.760
and cuts the elderly people's yards

00:57:54.760 --> 00:57:57.070
because they don't have
the means or ability

00:57:57.070 --> 00:57:59.650
to do it themselves and I
see little bitty things.

00:57:59.650 --> 00:58:02.600
Or even like the kids in California

00:58:02.600 --> 00:58:05.320
when the city dump sand
in their skate park,

00:58:05.320 --> 00:58:08.610
and they went out and
they cleaned the sand out

00:58:08.610 --> 00:58:09.810
of the skate park.

00:58:09.810 --> 00:58:12.520
It was one of the most
awesome things I've ever seen.

00:58:12.520 --> 00:58:16.330
That kind of stuff, that's
what brings me hope.

00:58:16.330 --> 00:58:18.870
And the smart aleckness of those kids,

00:58:18.870 --> 00:58:19.880
that's what brings me hope.

00:58:19.880 --> 00:58:20.783
I love that.

00:58:21.710 --> 00:58:24.750
The idea, the two women
who got busted in Laredo,

00:58:24.750 --> 00:58:26.390
and they ended up also getting freed

00:58:26.390 --> 00:58:27.980
by Texas Supreme Court order.

00:58:27.980 --> 00:58:30.650
They were cosmetologist doing
services in their homes.

00:58:30.650 --> 00:58:31.870
They're doing speakeasies.

00:58:31.870 --> 00:58:34.610
I mean, that's like a
prohibition era kind of thing.

00:58:34.610 --> 00:58:35.443
I love it.

00:58:35.443 --> 00:58:36.276
They were creative,

00:58:36.276 --> 00:58:37.660
and they were going around the man,

00:58:37.660 --> 00:58:39.033
that's an awesome thing.

00:58:40.190 --> 00:58:42.310
And the fact that Greg Abbott now says

00:58:42.310 --> 00:58:44.310
we can have home delivery of liquor kit.

00:58:44.310 --> 00:58:45.220
That's amazing.

00:58:45.220 --> 00:58:47.010
I think I've sent his office like a couple

00:58:47.010 --> 00:58:48.290
of emails saying that's cool.

00:58:48.290 --> 00:58:50.203
That will make this go away.

00:58:51.860 --> 00:58:53.630
- I thought you were gonna say
a couple of cases of whiskey,

00:58:53.630 --> 00:58:55.050
just a couple emails.

00:58:55.050 --> 00:58:56.890
- Oh, man, no, you can go and get ,

00:58:56.890 --> 00:58:58.840
what is it, one's a bourbon bloom kit

00:58:58.840 --> 00:59:02.200
and then you can actually get
like frozen margaritas now.

00:59:02.200 --> 00:59:03.033
And he's like,

00:59:03.033 --> 00:59:05.560
"Yeah, we may not ever have
these regulations come back in,"

00:59:05.560 --> 00:59:06.820
God bless Texas.

00:59:06.820 --> 00:59:08.880
So there's a little goofy things

00:59:08.880 --> 00:59:11.110
that I can point to, but ultimately.

00:59:11.110 --> 00:59:12.190
I am hopeful,

00:59:12.190 --> 00:59:15.510
it's hard to be a cynic when
you see that kind of stuff.

00:59:15.510 --> 00:59:16.343
And I am hopeful.

00:59:16.343 --> 00:59:18.200
And I know that there's enough
rabble-rousers out there

00:59:18.200 --> 00:59:20.993
and smart asses out there who really just,

00:59:22.130 --> 00:59:23.710
they give me hope.

00:59:23.710 --> 00:59:25.200
I don't know how else to put it,

00:59:25.200 --> 00:59:26.033
but they do.

